export const RUNBOOK_HELP="Client runbooks — original merchant accounting workspace\n\nUse merchant-accounting-workspace runbooks, or node workspace/server.mjs runbooks.\nChoose --url http://127.0.0.1:8446 for the running browser, or --workspace DIR for\nthe stopped original accounting workspace.\n\n  status | sources\n  book --id RUNBOOK\n  cycle --id PERIOD\n  operation --id REQUEST\n\n  prepare --action save --input /private/procedures.json --out /private/save.json\n  prepare --action attach --input /private/file-note.json --file /private/source.pdf --out /private/upload.json\n  prepare --action create --input /private/period.json --out /private/create.json\n  prepare --action assign --id PERIOD --input /private/responsibility-handover.json --out /private/assign.json\n  prepare --action work --id PERIOD --input /private/work.json --out /private/work-request.json\n  prepare --action submit --id PERIOD --input /private/handover.json --out /private/submit.json\n  prepare --action review --id PERIOD --input /private/review.json --out /private/review-request.json\n  prepare --action receive --input /private/operator.json --file /private/client-close.json --out /private/receive.json\n  execute --prepared /private/save.json\n  reconcile --prepared /private/save.json\n\n  download --id PERIOD --format packet --out /private/client-close.json\n  download --id PERIOD --format print --out /private/client-close.html\n  download --id PERIOD --format tasks --out /private/client-close-tasks.csv\n  file --id FILE --out /private/original-file.pdf\n\nPrepare retains a new exact native request, the current original workspace and\nrevision, route and digest. Its input JSON contains actor and the action's native\nfields; the command supplies workspaceId, requestId and revision. Execute or\nreconcile the SAME saved request after an interrupted response. Reconcile reports\nthe original committed result when present. NOT_FOUND retains the request for\nexact execution; it does not replace its identity. An explicit applied:false\nvalidation response lets you correct the input and prepare a new request.\n\nSelect original client close files or an explicit accountant handoff/revision. Preparation and review\nuse the same saved procedure edition. A received period retains its complete\nsource; its procedures can begin the next local period with an actual local close source.\nUploads are up to8MiB; complete portable JSON packets are up to64MiB. Supporting\nHTTPS links remain links, while selected uploaded files are carried in full.\nEvery output path must be new or already contain the exact same bytes.\n\nNamed procedure sets: save accepts profiles [{id,name,description,stepIds}] in the\nsaved edition. create accepts profileId from that edition; omit it to use every\nprocedure. The selected set remains fixed through preparation, review and handover.\nSee RUNBOOK_PROFILES.md and examples/weekly-monthly-runbook.json for the full setup.\n";
